{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at `e4f22d19ba32cce9de0c646d7ac0ec9337f7f44f`, tree `4789fd43`. A draw now opens the room again after a failed standing read, and that open reads the roster again. Two items below need an owner or a next edit, and neither blocks this landing.\n\n**Correction to my verdict `0c4800dc`.** I wrote that the person sees \"Refused because this key has no verified membership in this room.\" The Page does not show those words. `1-read-failed.json` and the baseline's `2-navigation-refused.json` show **Observation unknown** and \"The view could not be read.\" The builder's note says so. The stuck state itself was as I read it, and baseline-3 demonstrates it. The planner's phrase \"a valid member can be refused\" came from my wording.\n\n**What I checked.** I read the note, the diff, `openRoom` and `readerFor`. I ran `roster-refresh.scope.test.ts` and `assets.test.ts` once at this head: both pass, and the worktree stays clean. The manifest's seven units hold all 74 cited files with matching hashes, and all 11 table digests name those files. I checked the checksums and write modes of the four units behind this verdict (baseline-3, browser-2, checks and src), and they pass. My text scan of all seven units for link, key, JWT and bearer patterns found nothing. Workflow 41381703886 reports success at `658aab95`. `git diff --name-only 658aab95 e4f22d19` names four documents only, so the gate and the workflow carry.\n\n**The baseline ran first, and the repair distinguishes.** Baseline-3 at main `31384059` exits 0: after one aborted membership read, navigation stays on the failure screen with `membershipReads` still 1. Browser-2 exits 0 with 11 checks and no failures: the same step gives `membershipReads` 3, and `2-navigation-recovers.png` shows @ana, **Approve**, **Request changes**, and the comment form, unclipped. `control.log` reports exit 1 on \"THE NEXT DRAW cannot reuse the room whose standing failed\", then DISTINGUISHES. The note states that the launcher's outer exit is missing. The Page traffic holds one POST to `/acts`, at 03:12:25.059, before the first list capture at 03:12:25.281, and `browserActs` is empty from that capture on.\n\n**Architecture: sound.** `RoomOpening` stays generic, and the Page supplies its own guard. I walked the three cases that the request names:\n- **Pending reads:** a pending record has no `result`, so concurrent callers share it. The native witness asserts this.\n- **Late old reads:** `.then` writes `result` only to its own record, and the failure branch clears `current` only if that record is still current. A late refresh on the old room changes only the old room's `me`.\n- **Pending refresh:** `refreshRoster` keeps `me` during a read, so an in-flight refresh does not trigger a reopen. Only a completed failure or a completed roster without standing does.\n\n**Security: fails closed, with no new authority.** Reuse needs a current handle and the room's own key. Otherwise the draw makes a fresh `openRoom`, which requests a read session and reads the roster, and the result goes through `verifiedRoom` at `main.ts:1021`. A failed open rejects and clears the cache. No path restores standing except a completed roster, and the scope still judges each act. One cost: a key with no standing now makes a fresh open on each draw, where it once reused the cached room. Each open sends one `POST /sessions`, which browser-2's traffic shows once for the recovery. That cost is per navigation, and I see no loop that drives it, because a failed draw starts no observation.\n\n**Simplification: one change I recommend at the next edit of `shell.ts`.** The default `reusable = () =\u003e true` lets `new RoomOpening\u003cRoom\u003e()` compile. The test builds its own guard, and the browser witness lives only in the evidence unit. So removing `verifiedRoom` at `main.ts:149` would pass the gate and bring the stuck state back. Making the argument required lets the compiler hold that line, at the cost of one argument in `shell.test.ts`. The builder makes this change at its next edit of that file or says why not.\n\n**One item for the planner: the failure screen offers no way back.** `1-read-failed.html` holds two links: the wordmark to the homepage and **Join another room**. The witness navigates by script, and the note says so. A person has the browser's Back button or a reload. So this repair removes the need for a reload only if the person thinks to press Back, and neither case's words suggest it. The request's wording, \"recover the open Page\", is met at the draw level. A **Try again** control on that screen would finish it for a person. `e82c6550` already separates failed reads from unsupported definitions, so I recommend that it carries this. The ruling is yours.\n\n**How far this goes.** Local Worker, one Mac, one viewport, scripts, and routing that forces one failure. No deployed recovery and no person. Nothing assigns the earlier hosted stop this cause, and the note says so.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d117c200956c82c81913d07b214c0d69d5370162","binding":"assigned","head":"e4f22d19ba32cce9de0c646d7ac0ec9337f7f44f","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:05baf14dd28cfe9645b02939f4c5352d4c7fd23a\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:15c674b3060e9f2b7d995966b075432a3a317785\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:05baf14dd28cfe9645b02939f4c5352d4c7fd23a","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}